Drop a dead `ParsedExtensionMetaData parsed_metadata;` declaration in
the haybarn engine's `extension_load.cpp` that conflicts with the
`auto parsed_metadata = ParseExtensionMetaData(*handle);` later in
the same function. Only manifests as a compile error when the engine
is built with `WASM_LOADABLE_EXTENSIONS` (i.e. from this repo) — the
unused declaration is harmless in native builds, so the engine repo
doesn't carry this fix.

If/when the engine fork removes the dead declaration upstream, this
patch becomes a "previously applied" no-op and can be deleted.

diff --git a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
--- a/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
+++ b/src/main/extension/extension_load.cpp
@@ -374,7 +374,6 @@
 	auto filename = fs.ConvertSeparators(extension);

 	bool direct_load;
-	ParsedExtensionMetaData parsed_metadata;
 	ExtensionInstallMode install_mode = ExtensionInstallMode::UNKNOWN;

 	// shorthand case
